    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-2e6afcf73b47\",\"class\":\"partial\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"proof-secret-not-string-oneline\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\bProof\\\\b.*\\\\bsecret\\\\??\\\\s*:\\\\s*(Uint8Array|Buffer|ArrayBuffer|bytes|Bytes|Vec<u8>|\\\\[\\\\]byte|ByteArray|object|Record<)\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**\"},{\"id\":\"proof-c-lowercased-oneline\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\bProof\\\\b.*[{(,;]\\\\s*c\\\\??\\\\s*[:=](?!=)\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**\"}],\"coverage\":\"Flags added lines that name `Proof` and, on the same line, do one of two things. Either they type `secret` as a byte buffer, bytes or object type, or they name the `C` field in lower case as `c`.\",\"residual\":\"Does the hunk define, serialise or build Cashu proofs in a way that renames, omits or mistypes any of `amount` (int), `id` (hex string), `secret` (UTF-8 string) or `C` (hex string), beyond a one-line `Proof` declaration with a bytes or object `secret` or a lower-case `c` field?\",\"probes\":{\"violating\":[{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/cashu/proof.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+export type Proof = { amount: number; id: string; secret: Uint8Array; C: string };\\n\"},{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/cashu/proof.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+export type Proof = { amount: number; id: string; secret: string; c: string };\\n\"}],\"compliant\":{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/cashu/proof.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+export type Proof = { amount: number; id: string; secret: string; C: string };\\n\"}},\"rationale\":\"A line-based regex can only catch flagrant one-line `Proof` declarations or constructions with a bytes or object `secret` or a lower-case `c` key. Other cases need judgement: multi-line types, whether a structure really is a proof, omitted fields, wrong wire types, and serialisation logic. The file-extension scope cannot be fully expressed as one glob, so the constraints use `.floor/added/**`.\"}",
